m|first=Bill|date=March 28, 2022|url=https://theathletic.com/3213293/2022/03/28/oram-lebron-james-injury-in-loss-to-pelicans-could-be-the-biggest-lakers-collapse-of-all/|title=Oram: LeBron James' injury in loss to Pelicans could be the biggest Lakers collapse of all|website=The Athletic|access-date=April 10, 2022|archive-date=April 1, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220401131358/https://theathletic.com/3213293/2022/03/28/oram-lebron-james-injury-in-loss-to-pelicans-could-be-the-biggest-lakers-collapse-of-all/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Adams|first=Luke|date=March 28, 2022|url=https://www.hoopsrumors.com/2022/03/lebron-james-ankle-injury-feels-horrible.html|title=LeBron James: Ankle Injury Feels 'Horrible'|website=Hoops Rumors|access-date=April 10, 2022|archive-date=April 3, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220403202454/https://www.hoopsrumors.com/2022/03/lebron-james-ankle-injury-feels-horrible.html|url-status=live}}</ref>}} and the Lakers were eliminated from playoff and play-in contention for the first time since [[2018–19 Los Angeles Lakers season|2019]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=McMenamin|first=Dave|date=April 6, 2022|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/33680640/los-angeles-lakers-eliminated-playoff-contention-loss-phoenix-suns-win-san-antonio-spurs|title=Los Angeles Lakers eliminated from playoff contention after 7th straight loss|website=ESPN.com|access-date=April 6, 2022|archive-date=April 6, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220406051504/https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/33680640/los-angeles-lakers-eliminated-playoff-contention-loss-phoenix-suns-win-san-antonio-spurs|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|date=April 8, 2022 |title=Lakers' LeBron James to miss final 2 games of season to continue ankle sprain healing|url=https://theathletic.com/news/lakers-lebron-james-out-ankle-injury/k6ezPp8Gd4kx/ |access-date=April 10, 2022 |website=The Athletic}}</ref> James was named to the All-NBA Third Team for the second time; it was his 18th consecutive All-NBA Team selection, extending the record for most selections.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.nba.com/news/antetokounmpo-jokic-doncic-2021-22-kia-all-nba-first-team|title=Giannis Antetokounmpo, Nikola Jokic, Luka Doncic lead 2021–22 Kia All-NBA 1st Team|website=NBA.com|date=May 24, 2022|access-date=May 24, 2022}}</ref>

==== 2022–2023: All-time scoring record ====
In August 2022, James signed a two-year, $97&nbsp;million contract extension with the Lakers, which had a [[NBA salary cap#Options|player option]] in the second year.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|date=August 18, 2022 |title=Lakers Sign LeBron James to Contract Extension |url=https://www.nba.com/lakers/news/lakers-sign-lebron-james-to-contract-extension-220818 |access-date=August 20, 2022 |website=NBA.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Wojnarowski |first=Adrian |date=August 17, 2022 |title=LeBron lands 2-year, $97.1M deal with Lakers |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/34413561/lebron-james-los-angeles-lakers-agree-2-year-971-million-extension-includes-3rd-year-player-option |access-date=August 20, 2022 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> The contract brought his career earnings to $529&nbsp;million, an NBA record.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Winters |first=Mike |title=Already a billionaire, LeBron James' 2-year contract extension makes him the NBA's all-time highest-paid player |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2022/08/18/lebron-james-becomes-highest-paid-player-in-nba-history.html |access-date=August 20, 2022 |website=CNBC |date=August 18, 2022 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Gobert, Wolves extend Lakers' winless start with 111–102 win |url=https://africa.espn.com/nba/recap/_/gameId/401468231 |date=October 28, 2022|access-date=October 29, 2022|website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> On December 13, James scored 33 points in a 122–118 overtime loss to the Celtics, surpassing [[Wilt Chamberlain]] for the second-most 30-point games in NBA history, at 516.<ref>{{cite web |date=December 14, 2022 |title=LeBron James passes Wilt Chamberlain for 2nd-most 30-point games in NBA history |url=https://www.nba.com/news/lebron-james-passes-wilt-chamberlain-for-2nd-most-30-point-games-in-nba-history |access-date=December 14, 2022 |website=NBA.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Lakers laud 'amazing' LeBron James after 47-point birthday outing|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/35351037/lebron-james-season-high-47-38th-birthday-lakers-beat-hawks |date=December 30, 2022|access-date=December 31, 2022|website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref>

During January 2023, James recorded a string of accomplishments. He received his 66th [[NBA Player of the Month and Week|Player of the Week]] award; became the second player in NBA history to reach 38,000 points; achieved his 100th career game with 40 or more points scored; became the first player with a 40-point game against every NBA team; was named as a starter at the [[2023 NBA All-Star Game]], tying Kareem Abdul-Jabbar's record for the most All-Star selections with 19;{{Efn|It was also James' 19th consecutive All-Star appearance}} and became the first player in NBA history to post a triple-double in his 20th season.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron James, Donovan Mitchell named NBA Players of the Week |url=https://www.nba.com/news/nba-players-week-lebron-james-donovan-mitchell |access-date=January 9, 2023|website=nba.com}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron James becomes second player in NBA history to score 38,000 career points as Lakers star eyes record |url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-becomes-second-player-in-nba-history-to-score-38000-career-points-as-lakers-star-eyes-record/ |access-date=January 16, 2023 |website=NBA.com |date=January 16, 2023 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron drops 48, Lakers beat Rockets 140–132 to snap skid|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/recap/_/gameId/401468819 |date=January 16, 2023|access-date=January 18, 2023|website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|date=January 24, 2023 |title=LeBron scores 46 points with 9 3s, but Clippers rout Lakers |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/recap?gameId=401468874 |access-date=January 25, 2023 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Camras |first=Noah |title=Lakers News: LeBron James Makes Scoring History Tuesday Against Clippers |url=https://www.si.com/nba/lakers/news/lakers-news-lebron-james-makes-scoring-history-tuesday-against-clippers-nc2000 |access-date=January 25, 2023 |website=All Lakers {{!}} News, Rumors, Videos, Schedule, Roster, Salaries And More |date=January 25, 2023 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-surpasses-kobe-bryant-in-history-amid-nba-all-star-starter-not|title=LeBron James surpasses Kobe Bryant in history amid NBA All-Star starter nod|website=ClutchPoints|last=Yapkowitz|first=David|date=January 26, 2023|access-date=January 26, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-epic-performance-vs-knicks-reaches-heights-never-seen-nba-history|title=LeBron James' epic performance for Lakers vs. Knicks reaches heights never seen in NBA history|website=ClutchPoints|last=Guinhawa|first=Angelo|date=January 31, 2023|access-date=January 23, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-drops-steve-nash-from-top-4-of-assist-list-amid-scoring-chase|title=Lakers star LeBron James drops Steve Nash from Top 4 of assist list amid scoring chase|website=ClutchPoints|last=Guinhawa|first=Angelo|date=January 31, 2023|access-date=January 31, 2023}}</ref>}} On February 7, James passed Abdul-Jabbar as the [[List of NBA career scoring leaders|all-time leading scorer]] in NBA history.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-passes-fellow-lakers-legend-kareem-abdul-jabbar-for-most-points-in-nba-history |title=LeBron James passes fellow Lakers legend Kareem Abdul-Jabbar for most points in NBA history |website=ClutchPoints |last=Corvo |first=Michael |date=February 7, 2023 |access-date=February 7, 2023}}</ref> The NBA stopped the game with 10.9 seconds left in the third quarter for an on-court ceremony, during which James gave a speech and received the game ball from Abdul-Jabbar.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Watch: Kareem passes basketball to LeBron after breaking record |url=https://www.nbcsports.com/chicago/bulls/watch-kareem-abdul-jabbar-passes-basketball-lebron-james-after-breaking-record |access-date=February 21, 2023 |website=RSN |date=February 8, 2023 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.npr.org/2023/02/07/1152839238/lebron-james-nba-scoring-record-kareem-abdul-jabbar|title=LeBron James breaks the NBA career scoring record, passing Kareem Abdul-Jabbar|work=NPR|date=February 7, 2023|accessdate=February 7, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web| url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/35611846/lakers-lebron-james-passes-kareem-abdul-jabbar-become-nba-all-scoring-leader| title=LeBron James breaks Kareem Abdul-Jabbar's NBA scoring record| work=ESPN| date=February 7, 2023| accessdate=February 8, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|first=Dave |last=McMenamin|title=Sources: LeBron James feared out several weeks with foot injury|date=February 27, 2023|work=ESPN|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/35749430/sources-lebron-james-feared-several-weeks-foot-injury|access-date=February 28, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|first=Broderick|last=Turner|title=LeBron James is out tonight at Portland, expected back Wednesday|date=February 12, 2023|work=Los Angeles Times|url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2023-02-12/lebron-james-questionable-lakers-at-trail-blazers|access-date=February 28, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=2023 All-Star Draft & All-Star Game: Format, explainer and FAQ's|url=https://www.nba.com/news/2023-all-star-draft-all-star-game-explainer|website=NBA.com|access-date=February 3, 2023|date=February 6, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Quinn |first=Sam |date=February 20, 2023 |title=2023 NBA All-Star Game score: Jayson Tatum breaks scoring record, wins MVP; LeBron James' streak ends |url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/2023-nba-all-star-game-score-jayson-tatum-breaks-scoring-record-wins-mvp-lebron-james-streak-ends/live/ |access-date=February 21, 2023 |website=CBSSports.com}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.si.com/fannation/nba/fastbreak/injuries/los-angeles-lakers-lebron-james-hand-injury-in-2023-nba-all-star-game-video|title=VIDEO: LeBron James Appeared To Get Injured During NBA All-Star Game On This Play|first=Brett|last=Siegel|newspaper=Fastbreak on Fannation |date=February 19, 2023|access-date=April 12, 2023}}</ref>}}

James sustained a foot injury in late February, which caused him to miss 13 games.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last1=McMenamin |first1=Dave |title=LeBron James to monitor right foot after injury against Mavs |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/35743907/lebron-james-monitor-right-foot-injury-mavs |website=[[ESPN]] |date=February 27, 2023 |access-date=March 26, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last1=McMenamin |first1=Dave |title=LeBron James to have foot tendon injury reevaluated in 3 weeks |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/35769531/lebron-james-foot-tendon-injury-reevaluated-3-weeks |website=[[ESPN]] |date=March 2, 2023 |access-date=March 26, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last1=Greenawalt |first1=Tyler |title=LeBron James to return today vs. Bulls after 13-game absence |date=March 26, 2023 |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/lebron-james-to-return-today-vs-bulls-after-13-game-absence-185657919.html |publisher=Yahoo Sports |access-date=March 26, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Lakers' LeBron James: Will come off the bench Sunday |url=https://www.cbssports.com/fantasy/basketball/news/lakers-lebron-james-will-come-off-the-bench-sunday/ |work=CBS Sports |date=March 26, 2023 |access-date=March 26, 2023}}</ref>}} On April 2, he posted a triple-double during a 134–109 victory over the [[Houston Rockets]], tying [[Jason Kidd]] for fourth place on the all-time triple-doubles list.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-notches-historic-milestone-vs-rockets|title=Lakers star LeBron James notches another historic milestone in Rockets demolition job|website=ClutchPoints|last=Songco|first=Paolo|date=April 2, 2023|access-date=April 2, 2023}}</ref> James finished the regular season with averages of 28.9 points, 8.3 rebounds and 6.8 assists per game, becoming the oldest player in NBA history to average at least 25 points, five rebounds, and five assists in a season.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-completes-historic-feat-never-seen-before-as-year-20-comes-to-an-end|title=LeBron James completes historic feat never seen before as year 20 comes to an end|website=ClutchPoints|last=Yapkowitz|first=David|date=May 23, 2023|access-date=May 23, 2023}}</ref> In Game 4 of the first-round playoffs against the [[Memphis Grizzlies]], James had 22 points, a playoff career-high 20 rebounds, and seven assists in a 117–111 overtime victory, marking his first game ever with both 20 points scored and 20 rebounds.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron leads Lakers past Grizzlies 117–111 in OT for 3–1 lead |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/recap/_/gameId/401541184 |website=ESPN |access-date=April 25, 2023 |date=April 24, 2023}}</ref> He became the oldest player in league history with at least 20 points and 20 rebounds in a playoff game.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Lakers' LeBron James on 1st Career 20–20 Game: 'That's Pretty Cool, I Guess' |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/10073708-lakers-lebron-james-on-1st-career-20-20-game-thats-pretty-cool-i-guess |website=Bleacher Report |last=Wells |first=Adam |access-date=April 27, 2023 |date=April 25, 2023}}</ref> In Game 6 of the Western Conference semifinals, James put up 30 points, nine rebounds, nine assists and two steals, in a 122–101 victory over the [[Golden State Warriors|Warriors]] to lead the Lakers to the Western Conference finals. He also won his 41st playoff series, surpassing [[Derek Fisher]] for the most playoff series wins in NBA history.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-anthony-davis-share-emotional-moment-warriors-win|title=WATCH: Lakers stars LeBron James, Anthony Davis share emotional moment after beating Warriors|website=ClutchPoints|last=Songco|first=Paolo|date=May 12, 2023|access-date=May 12, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-passes-la-icon-for-playoff-record-and-it-isnt-kobe-bryant-or-kareem-abdul-jabbar|title=LeBron James passes Lakers icon for playoff record, and it isn't Kobe Bryant or Kareem Abdul-Jabbar|website=ClutchPoints|last=Guinhawa|first=Angelo|date=May 12, 2023|access-date=May 12, 2023}}</ref> In the Western Conference finals, the Lakers were swept by the [[Denver Nuggets|Nuggets]], who would go on to win the [[2023 NBA Finals|championship]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/recap/_/gameId/401547684|title=Jokic leads Denver Nuggets past LeBron's Lakers 113–111, into their first NBA Finals|website=ESPN.com.|date=May 22, 2023|accessdate=May 24, 2023}}</ref>

====2023–2024: NBA Cup MVP and 40K points====
[[File:LeBron James, 25 November 2023 03.jpg|thumb|James shooting a [[fadeaway]] against the Cavaliers in [[Cleveland]] in 2023]]
For the [[2023–24 NBA season|2023–24 season]], James switched back to jersey No. 23 from No. 6 in honor of [[Bill Russell]], who had died the previous year and whose No. 6 jersey had been retired league-wide.<ref>{{Cite web |last=McMenamin |first=Dave |date=2023-07-16 |title=LeBron to go back to No. 23 in honor of Russell |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/38016718/lebron-james-change-jersey-number-back-23-honor-bill-russell |access-date=2025-06-09 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> With the retirements of [[Udonis Haslem]] and Andre Iguodala, James became the NBA's [[List of oldest and youngest NBA players|oldest active player]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Reynolds |first=Tim |date=October 20, 2023 |url=https://www.nba.com/news/lebron-james-numbers-season-21 |title=Inside the numbers: LeBron James is now the NBA's oldest player |agency=Associated Press |website=NBA.com |access-date=October 21, 2023}}</ref> On November 15, James logged 28 points, 10 rebounds and 11 assists in a 125–110 loss to the [[Sacramento Kings]], becoming the second-oldest player to record a triple-double.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Reedy |first=Joe |url=https://apnews.com/article/rockets-lakers-e95e43d759cb81d3de96bf131b9345e6 |title=James scores season-high 37, hits go-ahead free throw as Lakers hold off Rockets 105–104 |work=Associated Press News |date=November 20, 2023 |access-date=November 20, 2023}}</ref> In November, James became the first player in NBA history to reach 5,000 career turnovers.<ref name="e060">{{cite web | last=Quinn | first=Sam | title=WATCH: LeBron James becomes first player in NBA history to reach 5,000 turnovers | website=CBSSports.com | date=2023-11-11 | url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-becomes-first-player-in-nba-history-to-reach-5000-turnovers/ | access-date=2025-06-21}}</ref> On November 27, in a 138–94 loss to the Philadelphia 76ers, James surpassed [[Kareem Abdul-Jabbar]] to become the player with the most minutes played in NBA games during the regular season and playoffs.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rosa |first=Francisco |title=Lakers' LeBron James Passes Kareem Abdul-Jabbar to Set NBA Minutes Record |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/10098909-lakers-lebron-james-passes-kareem-abdul-jabbar-to-set-nba-minutes-record |access-date=November 28, 2023 |website=Bleacher Report |language=en}}</ref> The 44-point loss was the worst of James's career.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-suffers-worst-defeat-in-nba-career-as-embiid-76ers-rout-lakers-by-44-points/ |title=LeBron James suffers worst defeat in NBA career as Embiid, 76ers rout Lakers by 44 points |agency=Associated Press |publisher=CBS News |date=November 28, 2023 |access-date=November 28, 2023}}</ref> On December 9, James and the Lakers won the [[2023 NBA In-Season Tournament|inaugural NBA In-Season Tournament]], with James receiving the Tournament MVP award and being selected to the All-Tournament team.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bontemps |first=Tim |date=December 9, 2023 |title=Lakers win NBA Cup; LeBron James earns in-season tournament MVP |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/39080368/lakers-win-nba-cup-lebron-james-earns-season-tournament-mvp |access-date=November 28, 2023 |website=ESPN |language=en}}</ref>

On January 25, 2024, James was named an All-Star starter for the [[2024 NBA All-Star Game]], marking his 20th NBA All-Star selection, surpassing Abdul-Jabbar for the most All-Star selections.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://clutchpoints.com/nba-all-star-game-2024-starters-lebron-james-giannis-antetokounmpo |title=2024 NBA All-Star Game starters: LeBron James earns league-record 20th appearance |website=ClutchPoints |last=Siegel |first=Brett |date=January 25, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240127045124/https://clutchpoints.com/nba-all-star-game-2024-starters-lebron-james-giannis-antetokounmpo |archive-date=January 27, 2024 |url-status=live |access-date=January 25, 2024}}</ref> On February 28, James led the Lakers to a 116–112 comeback win against the [[Clippers (NBA Team)|Clippers]]. Trailing by 21 points entering the fourth quarter, he outscored the Clippers by himself 19–16 in the final quarter, going 5-for-8 from three-point range. It was the largest fourth-quarter comeback of James's career.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Botkin |first=Brad |url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-single-handedly-outscores-clippers-in-fourth-quarter-as-lakers-come-back-from-21-point-deficit/ |title=LeBron James single-handedly outscores Clippers in fourth quarter as Lakers come back from 21-point deficit |work=[[CBS Sports]] |date=March 1, 2024 |access-date=March 4, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=McMenamin |first1=Dave |title=LeBron James powers biggest 4th-quarter comeback of career |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/39621969/lebron-james-powers-biggest-4th-quarter-comeback-career |website=ESPN.com |date=February 29, 2024 |access-date=February 29, 2024}}</ref> Three days later, James became the first player in NBA history to reach 40,000 career points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Woike |first=Dan |url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2024-03-02/lebron-james-40000-points-milestone-lakers-nuggets |title=LeBron James becomes first NBA player to score 40,000 points in Lakers' loss to Nuggets |work=[[Los Angeles Times]] |date=March 2, 2024 |access-date=November 7, 2024}}</ref> On March 16, he scored a season-high 40 points in a loss to the Warriors.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Woike |first1=Dan |title=Anthony Davis injury overshadows LeBron James' 40 points in loss to Warriors |url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2024-03-16/anthony-davis-lebron-james-lakers-warriors-recap |website=[[Los Angeles Times]] |access-date=March 16, 2024}}</ref> On March 31, he put up 40 points on a career-high nine 3-pointers in a 116–104 victory over the [[Brooklyn Nets]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-brooklyn-nets-3-point-shooting-los-angeles |title='Masterful' LeBron James' leads Lakers over Nets with career-best 3-point shooting night |website=ClutchPoints |last=Corvo |first=Michael |date=March 31, 2024 |access-date=March 31, 2024}}</ref> On April 2, James passed [[Oscar Schmidt]] to become [[List of basketball players with most career points|the world's all-time scoring leader in basketball history]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/lebron-james-surpassed-oscar-schmidt-075718103.html |title=LeBron James surpassed Oscar Schmidt to become world's all-time scoring leader |website=sports.yahoo.com |date=April 5, 2024 |access-date=October 27, 2024}}</ref> James finished his 21st season in the NBA averaging 25.7 points, 8.3 assists and 7.3 rebounds a game. He shot 54% from the field and a career-high 41% from 3-point range.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Marvi |first1=Robert |title=Some amazing facts about LeBron James' 2023–24 regular season stats |url=https://lebronwire.usatoday.com/2024/04/15/some-amazing-facts-about-lebron-james-2023-24-regular-season-stats/ |website=lebronwire.usatoday.com |date=April 15, 2024 |access-date=May 3, 2024}}</ref>

====2024–2025: First father-son duo====
On July 6, 2024, James re-signed with the Lakers on a two-year, $104 million contract which carried a [[no-trade clause]] and had a player option in the second year.<ref>{{cite web |title=Los Angeles Lakers Re-Sign Lebron James |url=https://www.nba.com/lakers/news/los-angeles-lakers-re-sign-lebron-james-70624 |website=NBA.com |date=July 6, 2024 |access-date=July 14, 2024}}</ref> James's son [[Bronny]] had been drafted 55th by the Lakers; on October 22, in a game against the [[Minnesota Timberwolves]], James and Bronny became the first father-son duo to play in an NBA game together.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{Cite web |date=June 27, 2024 |title=From Luke and Bill Walton to LeBron and Bronny James, these are the top NBA father-son duos |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/38955259/nba-top-father-son-duos-james-walton-thompson-curry-sabonis |access-date=July 15, 2024 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://clutchpoints.com/lakers-news-lebron-james-bronny-james-nba-history-timberwolves |title=Lakers' LeBron James, Bronny James make NBA history vs. Timberwolves |last=Finnegan |first=Troy |website=ClutchPoints |date=October 22, 2024 |access-date=October 22, 2024}}</ref><ref name="ESPNBronny2024">{{cite news|title=LeBron and Bronny James make NBA history by playing together in Lakers' 110–103 win over Minnesota|date=October 22, 2024|publisher=ESPN|agency=AP|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/recap/_/gameId/401704628|access-date=October 24, 2024}}</ref><ref name="Dave McMenamin">{{cite web |last1=McMenamin |first1=Dave |date=June 27, 2024 |title=Lakers pick Bronny James in second round of NBA draft |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/40447437/lakers-pick-bronny-james-second-round-nba-draft |access-date=June 27, 2024 |website=ESPN.com}}</ref>}} On November 13, James logged a triple-double against the [[Memphis Grizzlies|Grizzlies]], setting a new record for the oldest player to record a triple-double in three consecutive games.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Quinn |first=Sam |url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-records-third-consecutive-triple-double-breaks-his-own-record-as-lakers-beat-grizzlies/ |title=LeBron James records third consecutive triple-double, breaks his own record as Lakers beat Grizzlies |work=[[CBS Sports]] |date=November 14, 2024 |access-date=November 14, 2024}}</ref> Two days later, he recorded his fourth consecutive triple-double of the season, breaking his own record for the most consecutive triple-doubles.<ref>{{Cite web |last=McMenamin |first=Dave |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/42418548/lebron-james-posts-4th-straight-triple-double-lakers-win |title=LeBron James posts 4th straight triple-double in Lakers' win |publisher=[[ESPN]] |date=November 16, 2024 |access-date=November 16, 2024}}</ref> On December 1, James became only the second player (after Kareem Abdul-Jabbar) to score 15,000 career field goals, and on December 19 he passed Abdul-Jabbar for the most regular season minutes played in a career.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/nba/top-stories/lebron-james-makes-nba-history-as-second-player-to-reach-15000-field-goals/articleshow/115892196.cms |title=LeBron James Makes NBA History As Second Player To Reach 15,000 Field Goals |work=[[The Times of India]] |date=December 2, 2024 |access-date=December 3, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=December 19, 2024 |title=Lakers star LeBron James breaks NBA record for career minutes |url=https://www.nba.com/news/lebron-james-breaks-nba-record-career-minutes |access-date=March 7, 2026 |website=NBA.com}}</ref>

On January 3, 2025, James put up 30 points and eight assists in a 119–102 win over the [[Atlanta Hawks|Hawks]], surpassing Michael Jordan for the most 30-point regular season games in NBA history.<ref>{{Cite web |last=McMenamin |first=Dave |date=2025-01-04 |title=LeBron James breaks Michael Jordan's record for 30-point games |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/43279592/lakers-lebron-james-breaks-michael-jordan-record-30-point-games |access-date=2026-02-21 |website=ESPN}}</ref> On February 6, James recorded a season-high 42 points in a win over the Warriors, making James the oldest player to score 40 or more points in a game.<ref>{{Cite web |date=February 7, 2025 |title=Starting 5, Feb. 7: LeBron, Steph & a (new) all-time duel, Ant can't stop |url=https://www.nba.com/news/starting-5-feb-7-2025-2 |access-date=March 7, 2026 |website=NBA.com}}</ref> James was selected for his [[2025 NBA All-Star Game|21st NBA All-Star Game]], but missed the game due to foot and ankle soreness, which ended his streak of 20 consecutive All-Star game starts.<ref>{{cite news|first=Dan|last=Woike|title=LeBron James won't play in NBA All-Star Game, ending his 20-year streak|date=February 16, 2025|newspaper=Los Angeles Times|url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2025-02-16/lakers-star-lebron-james-misses-21st-all-star-game|access-date=February 17, 2025}}</ref> On March 4, James surpassed 50,000 career points across the regular season and playoffs.<ref>{{cite web |date=March 4, 2025 |title=Lakers star LeBron James surpasses 50,000 combined points in regular season and playoffs |url=https://www.nba.com/news/lakers-lebron-james-surpasses-50000-total-points |access-date=March 5, 2025 |website=NBA.com|agency=Associated Press}}</ref> Four days later, he experienced a groin injury, which kept him off the court for seven games.<ref>{{cite news |title=Report: LeBron James expected to miss time after suffering groin injury vs. Celtics |url=https://www.nba.com/news/lebron-james-groin-injury |access-date=March 15, 2025 |work=NBA.com |date=March 9, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Beacham |first1=Greg |title=LeBron James returns from 7-game absence as Bulls dismantle Lakers |url=https://www.nba.com/news/lebron-james-starts-in-return-from-his-7-game-injury-absence-when-lakers-face-bulls |access-date=March 23, 2025 |work=NBA.com |date=March 22, 2025}}</ref> On March 26, he scored 13 points and a game-winning [[buzzer-beater]] in a 120–119 victory against the [[Indiana Pacers|Pacers]].<ref>{{Cite magazine|last=Phillips|first=Ryan|url=https://www.si.com/nba/lebron-james-buzzer-beater-tip-in-vs-pacers|title=LeBron James Saves Brutal Statistical Night With Buzzer Beater Tip-In vs. Pacers|magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]]|date=March 26, 2025|access-date=March 27, 2025}}</ref> The Lakers were eliminated in the first round of the playoffs for the second straight year.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Woike|first=Dan|url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2025-04-30/los-angeles-lakers-minnesota-timberwolves-nba-playoff-game-5|title=Lakers' season comes to a disappointing end with first-round loss to Timberwolves|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|date=April 30, 2025|access-date=May 3, 2025}}</ref> In the deciding game 5 loss to the [[Minnesota Timberwolves|Timberwolves]], James sprained the [[medial collateral ligament]] in his left knee. He spent the next several months focused on recovery in preparation for the Lakers' September training camp.<ref>{{cite news|title=LeBron James says knee 'good,' targeting 100% by training camp|date=June 17, 2025|work=ESPN|url=http://espn.com/nba/story/_/id/45528391/lakers-lebron-james-says-injured-knee-feeling-good-targeting-close-100-percent-possible-training-camp|access-date=June 19, 2025}}</ref>

====2025–2026: Final season in Los Angeles====
[[File:LeBron James (55095816551) (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright=0.70|James with the Los Angeles Lakers in 2026]]
After missing the Lakers' first 14 games due to [[sciatica]], James made his season debut on November 18 in a 140–126 win over the [[Utah Jazz]]. He became the first player to play in 23 NBA seasons.<ref>{{cite web |last=Sanghera |first=Mandeep |date=November 19, 2025 |title=James breaks NBA record with first game of season |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/basketball/articles/ckg4kedp42po |publisher=[[BBC News]] |access-date=February 17, 2026}}</ref> On December 4, in a 123–120 win over the [[Toronto Raptors]], James assisted on [[Rui Hachimura]]'s game-winning, buzzer-beating 3-pointer, finishing the game with eight points.<ref>{{cite news|first=Jack|last=Baer|title=LeBron James' incredible 10-point streak ends after 1,297 games and nearly 19 years|date=December 4, 2025|website=Yahoo Sports|url= https://sports.yahoo.com/article/lebron-james-incredible-10-point-031155818.html|access-date=December 5, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|first=Thuc Nhi|last=Nguyen|title=LeBron James' record scoring streak ends, but Austin Reaves and Rui Hachimura deliver win|date=December 4, 2025|newspaper=Los Angeles Times|url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2025-12-04/los-angeles-lakers-toronto-raptors-nba-game-recap|access-date=December 4, 2025}}</ref> This ended his record-making streak of 1,297 consecutive games with at least 10 points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Duarte |first=Michael |date=December 5, 2025 |title=This is what the world looked like the last time LeBron James scored single digits: iPhones didn't exist and nobody had heard of Rihanna yet |url=https://www.nbclosangeles.com/news/sports/this-is-what-the-world-looked-like-the-last-time-lebron-james-scored-single-digits-iphones-didnt-exist-and-nobody-had-heard-of-rihanna-yet/3811919/ |publisher=[[NBC Los Angeles]] |access-date=January 3, 2026}}</ref> James passed Kobe Bryant to become the player with the most double-doubles with 30+ points in Lakers franchise history.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Beacham |first=Greg |date=January 14, 2026 |title=LeBron just misses historic triple-double, but still defies his age with prolific efforts for Lakers |url=https://apnews.com/article/lebron-james-lakers-triple-double-e9ab8476c6d929c6201fd25ea4a48258 |publisher=[[Associated Press News]] |access-date=January 14, 2026}}</ref>

After sitting out a game against the [[San Antonio Spurs]] on February 10, James became ineligible from receiving any regular season awards by missing his 18th game of the season. As a result, his record streak of 21 consecutive [[All-NBA Team]] selections came to an end.<ref>{{cite news |last1=McMenamin |first1=Dave |title=Lakers' LeBron James sits out loss to Spurs, ending All-NBA run |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/47890359/lakers-rule-lebron-james-foot-ending-all-nba-streak |access-date=13 February 2026 |work=ESPN |date=10 February 2026 |language=en}}</ref> On February 12, he became the oldest player in NBA history to post a triple-double, recording 28 points, 12 assists, and 10 rebounds in a victory over the [[2025–26 Dallas Mavericks season|Dallas Mavericks]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Beacham |first1=Greg |title=LeBron James becomes oldest player with triple-double in Lakers' 124-104 win over Mavericks |url=https://apnews.com/article/lakers-mavericks-score-lebron-james-63078e79426fe55b5656a221a7821249 |access-date=13 February 2026 |work=AP News |date=12 February 2026 |language=en}}</ref> On February 28, James reached 1,000 three-pointers made as a Laker.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/nba/los-angeles-lakers/lakers-news-lebron-james-joins-kobe-bryant-historic-la-club|title=Lakers' LeBron James joins Kobe Bryant in historic LA club|website=ClutchPoints|last=Binoy|first=Allan|date=February 28, 2026|access-date=February 28, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://sports.yahoo.com/nba/breaking-news/article/lebron-james-joins-kobe-bryant-as-second-player-to-make-1000-3-pointers-with-lakers-starts-hot-in-win-over-warriors-025445071.html|title=LeBron James joins Kobe Bryant as second player to make 1,000 3-pointers with Lakers, starts hot in win over Warriors|website=Yahoo Sports|last=Backstrom|first=Andy|date=February 28, 2026|access-date=February 28, 2026}}</ref> On March 5, in a game against the [[Denver Nuggets]], James made his 15,838th career [[Field goal (basketball)|field goal]] and surpassed [[Kareem Abdul-Jabbar]] for the most career field goals made in NBA history.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/nba/los-angeles-lakers/lakers-news-lebron-james-wholesome-reaction-breaking-all-time-field-goals-record|title=Lakers' LeBron James shares wholesome reaction to breaking all-time field goals made record|website=ClutchPoints|last=Binoy|first=Allan|date=March 5, 2026|access-date=March 5, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/48117860/lebron-james-passes-kareem-abdul-jabbar-most-made-fg-nba-history|title=LeBron James passes Kareem Abdul-Jabbar for most made FG in NBA history|website=espn.com|last=McMenamin|first=Dave|date=March 5, 2026|access-date=March 5, 2026}}</ref> On March 21, James played his 1,612th career game, passing [[Robert Parish]] to become the [[List of NBA career games played leaders|all-time leader in career games played]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Nguyen |first=Thuc Nhi |date=March 21, 2026 |title=Luke Kennard sinks last-second three-pointer as Lakers win ninth straight game |url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/lakers/story/2026-03-21/los-angeles-lakers-orlando-magic-game-recap-lebron-james-record |work=[[Los Angeles Times]] |access-date=March 22, 2026}}</ref> Ten days later, James surpassed Abdul-Jabbar for the most career wins in NBA history, with 1,229.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://sports.yahoo.com/nba/article/lebron-james-passes-kareem-abdul-jabbar-for-most-wins-in-nba-history-050708430.html|title=LeBron James passes Kareem Abdul-Jabbar for most wins in NBA history|website=Yahoo Sports|last=Baer|first=Jack|date=April 1, 2026|access-date=April 11, 2026}}</ref> On April 10, James recorded his 12,000th career assist in a game against the [[Phoenix Suns]], joining [[Jason Kidd]], [[Chris Paul]], and [[John Stockton]] as the only players to record at least 12,000 career assists in NBA history.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://clutchpoints.com/nba/los-angeles-lakers/lakers-news-lebron-james-joins-jason-kidd-chris-paul-historic-assist-club|title=Lakers' LeBron James joins Jason Kidd, Chris Paul in historic assist club|website=ClutchPoints|last=Imran|first=Abdullah|date=April 11, 2026|access-date=April 11, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/lebron-james-becomes-4th-nba-player-reach-12000-career-assists--flm-2026-04-11/|title=LeBron James becomes 4th NBA player to reach 12,000 career assists|website=Reuters|date=April 11, 2026|access-date=April 11, 2026}}</ref> On May 7, he became the first NBA player to play in 300 playoff games.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Espinal |first=Nelson |date=2026-05-08 |title=LeBron James Hits Rare Playoff Milestone in Lakers Series vs. Thunder |url=https://lasportsreport.com/lakers/253830/lebron-james-hits-rare-playoff-milestone-in-lakers-series-vs-thunder/ |access-date=2026-05-08 |website=LA Sports Report |language=en-US}}</ref> On June 30, it was announced that James had informed the Lakers that he would not be returning to the team for the [[2026–27 Los Angeles Lakers season|2026–27 season]].<ref>{{cite news |date=June 30, 2026 |title=LeBron James informs Lakers he plans to play elsewhere in 2026-27 |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/nba/story/_/id/49226472/lebron-james-informs-lakers-plans-play-elsewhere-2026-27 |access-date=June 30, 2026 |work=ESPN}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Zimmerman |first=Kevin |date=June 30, 2026 |title=LeBron James says goodbye to the Lakers |url=https://arizonasports.com/nba/lebron-james-says-goodbye-lakers-free-agency-news |access-date=June 30, 2026 |website=Arizona Sports |language=en}}</ref>

===Philadelphia 76ers (2026–present)===
On July 24, 2026, James announced on [[X (social network)|X]] that he would be signing with the [[Philadelphia 76ers]], calling it his "last decision".<ref>{{Cite web |title=LeBron James announces he is signing with 76ers |url=https://www.nba.com/news/lebron-james-free-agency-sixers-2026 |access-date=2026-07-25 |website=NBA.com|date=2026-07-24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260725085432/https://www.nba.com/news/lebron-james-free-agency-sixers-2026|archive-date=2026-07-25|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Vardon |first=Joe |last2=Jones |first2=Tony |last3=Woike |first3=Dan |last4=Aldridge |first4=David |date=2026-07-24 |title=LeBron James signing with Philadelphia 76ers, marking his record 24th season |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7417464/2026/07/24/lebron-james-contract-76ers-free-agency/ |access-date=2026-07-25 |work=The New York Times |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Following the announcement, Pennsylvania governor [[Josh Shapiro]] declared July 24 "LeBron James Day" throughout the state.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Hendrickson|first=Beccah|title=Pennsylvania marks LeBron James Day as leaders celebrate star's announcement|url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/pennsylvania-marks-lebron-james-day-023205585.html|date=2026-07-25}}</ref> On July 26, James signed a 2-year, $8 million contract, which includes a player option.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Jones |first=Tony |last2=Bartholomew |first2=Rafe |date=2026-07-26 |title=LeBron James' signing with 76ers is official, per NBA |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7471625/2026/07/26/lebron-james-sixers-deal-official-dalen-terry-waived/ |access-date=2026-07-27 |work=[[The New York Times]] |issn=0362-4331|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260727152227/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7471625/2026/07/26/lebron-james-sixers-deal-official-dalen-terry-waived/|archive-date=2026-07-27|url-status=live|publisher=[[The Athletic]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Philadelphia 76ers Sign 4x NBA Champion and 22x All-Star LeBron James|url=https://www.nba.com/sixers/news/philadelphia-76ers-sign-4x-nba-champion-and-22x-all-star-lebron-james|website=[[National Basketball Association|NBA.com]]|access-date=July 27, 2026|date=July 27, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260727155526/https://www.nba.com/web/20260727155526//sixers/news/philadelphia-76ers-sign-4x-nba-champion-and-22x-all-star-lebron-james|archive-date=July 27, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>

==National team career==
[[File:LeBron James vs Yao Ming - Olympics 2008.jpg|thumb|James attempting a shot over China's [[Yao Ming]] at the [[2008 Summer Olympics]]]]
As a 19-year-old rookie, James made his debut for the [[United States men's national basketball team|United States national team]] at the [[2004 United States men's Olympic basketball team|2004 Olympics]] in Athens, Greece, although he spent most of the event on the bench.<ref name="USA">{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron James Bio|url=http://www.usabasketball.com/bios/james_lebron.html|publisher=USA Basketball|access-date=February 26, 2013|archive-date=July 10, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130710085235/http://www.usabasketball.com/bios/james_lebron.html|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="Thamel-2008">{{Cite news |last=Thamel |first=Pete |date=2008-07-28 |title=After Sitting in 2004, Ready to Stand and Deliver |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2008/07/28/sports/olympics/28hoops.html |access-date=2026-02-26 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Team USA finished with a bronze medal, becoming the first U.S. basketball team to return home without a gold medal since the NBA started allowing active players to participate in the Olympics.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|agency=Associated Press|title=U.S.: 3-for-24 from 3-point range|url=https://www.espn.com/olympics/summer04/basketball/news/story?id=1859825|website=ESPN|date=August 15, 2004 |access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> James felt he was not given "a fair opportunity to play".<ref name="Thamel-2008" />

At the [[2006 FIBA World Championship]] in Japan, James took on a greater role for Team USA, averaging 13.9 points, 4.8 rebounds, and 4.1 assists per game as co-captain.<ref name="usabbb">{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.usabasketball.com/seniormen/2006/06_mwc_cumulative_stats.html|title=2006 USA Men's World Championship Team (8–1)|publisher=USA Basketball|access-date=May 1, 2007|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070513145308/http://www.usabasketball.com/seniormen/2006/06_mwc_cumulative_stats.html|archive-date=May 13, 2007}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|website=NBA.com|url=http://www.nba.com/nuggets/news/anthony_usa_captain_081706.html|title=Carmelo Anthony Named One of Three USA World Championship Team Captains|access-date=May 7, 2007|date=August 17, 2006}}</ref> The team finished the tournament with an 8–1 record, winning another bronze medal.<ref name="usabbb"/> During this time, James was known for his disrespectful attitude toward the national team's staff, coaches and players. While assembling the [[2008 United States men's Olympic basketball team|2008 Olympic squad]], Team USA managing director [[Jerry Colangelo]] and coach [[Mike Krzyzewski]] told James he could only play if he improved his attitude, and James complied. Colangelo said that James matured significantly as both a player and a person as a result of the ultimatum.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wojnarowski |first=Adrian |date=September 3, 2007 |title=Team USA's declaration of independence |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/nba/news/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160307110240/https://sports.yahoo.com/nba/news?slug=aw-teamusa090307 |archive-date=March 7, 2016 |access-date=2026-02-27 |website=Yahoo Sports}}</ref><ref name="wojnarowski_08122012">{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Wojnarowski|first=Adrian|author-link=Adrian Wojnarowski|title=Season of LeBron ends with Olympic gold medal|date=August 12, 2012|publisher=Yahoo! Sports|url=https://sports.yahoo.com/news/nba--season-of-lebron-ends-with-olympic-gold-medal.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120815052130/http://sports.yahoo.com/news/nba--season-of-lebron-ends-with-olympic-gold-medal.html|archive-date=August 15, 2012|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Helin|first=Kurt|title=USA Basketball president lauds LeBron James' maturity|date=August 14, 2012|publisher=NBC Sports|url=https://nba.nbcsports.com/2012/08/14/usa-basketball-president-lauds-lebron-james-maturity/|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref>}}

At the [[FIBA Americas Championship 2007]], James put up 31 points against Argentina in the championship game, the most ever by an American in an Olympic qualifier.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|website=ESPN|url=https://www.espn.com/olympics/olybb/news/story?id=3002435|title=James' record outing highlights Team USA's dominance in title game|date=September 2, 2007|access-date=December 22, 2021|agency=Associated Press}}</ref> Team USA went 10–0, winning the championship and qualifying for the [[2008 Olympics]] in [[Beijing]],<ref name="USA" /> where they went undefeated and won the gold medal.<ref name="Morgan2016">{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Morgan|first=Chris|url=https://www.pastemagazine.com/olympics/the-olympics/that-one-time-they-lost-on-the-team-usa-mens-baske/|title=That One Time They Lost: On the Team USA Men's Basketball Disaster in Athens|magazine=Paste|date=August 17, 2016|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref><ref name="Spain">{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.basketball-reference.com/olympics/games/2008-08-24-USA-ESP/|title=United States vs. Spain, August 24, 2008 – Final Round|access-date=February 20, 2018|website=Basketball Reference|publisher=Sports Reference}}</ref>

[[File:Mansoor Ahmed photos of Team USA basketball at London 2012 Olympics.jpg|thumb|left|upright|James attempting a dunk at the [[2012 Summer Olympics]]]]
James did not play at the [[2010 United States men's FIBA World Championship team|2010 FIBA World Championship]] but became the leader of Team USA ahead of the [[2012 United States men's Olympic basketball team|2012 Olympics]] in London.<ref name="ap_column">{{#invoke:cite|news|title=Column: Going out in style – 'K Boys' golden again|date=August 12, 2012|website=ESPN|agency=Associated Press|url=http://www.espn.com/espn/wire?section=oly&id=8262281|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140714233540/http://sports.espn.go.com/espn/wire?section=oly&id=8262281|archive-date=July 14, 2014|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|agency=Reuters|title=LeBron, Kobe return to U.S. team for London Games|url=https://www.chicagotribune.com/ct-xpm-2012-07-07-sns-rt-us-teambre867000-20120707-story.html|newspaper=Chicago Tribune|access-date=December 22, 2021|date=July 7, 2012}}</ref> During a game against [[Australia men's national basketball team|Australia]], he recorded the first triple-double in U.S. Olympic basketball history with 11 points, 14 rebounds, and 12 assists.{{efn|Assists were recorded as an official Olympic statistic starting in 1976.<ref name=triple_double>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron James Tallies First Triple-Double in U.S. Olympic History To Power USA To Semifinals With 119–86 Win Against Australia|date=August 8, 2012|publisher=USA Basketball|url=http://www.usabasketball.com/mens/national/12_moly_game_06.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120810210413/http://www.usabasketball.com/mens/national/12_moly_game_06.html|archive-date=August 10, 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref>}} Team USA won the gold medal, again defeating Spain in the final game.<ref name="Spain2">{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Stein|first=Marc|title=Team USA as good as gold again|url=http://www.espn.com/olympics/summer/2012/basketball/story/_/id/8262102/2012-olympics-team-usa-good-gold-again|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=October 14, 2018|date=August 12, 2012}}</ref> James contributed 19 points in the victory, becoming the all-time leading scorer in U.S. men's basketball history.<ref name=USA/><ref name=Spain2/> He became the second player, alongside Michael Jordan, to win an NBA MVP award, NBA championship, NBA Finals MVP, and Olympic gold medal in the same year.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://hangtime.blogs.nba.com/2012/08/12/u-s-surges-past-spain-late-claims-second-straight-olympic-gold-medal/|title=U.S. Surges Past Spain Late, Claims Second Straight Olympic Gold Medal|first=Sekou|last=Smith|date=August 12, 2012|access-date=August 13, 2012|website=NBA.com|archive-date=November 26, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151126163535/http://hangtime.blogs.nba.com/2012/08/12/u-s-surges-past-spain-late-claims-second-straight-olympic-gold-medal/|url-status=dead}}</ref>

After a 12-year hiatus from the Olympics, James joined the [[2024 United States men's Olympic basketball team|2024 Olympic squad]] in Paris as team captain at 39 years old.<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 30, 2024 |title=LeBron James Has 'Captain LeMerica' Nickname Added to Basketball-Reference Profile |website=[[Bleacher Report]] |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/10130181-lebron-james-has-captain-lemerica-nickname-added-to-basketball-reference-profile}}</ref> He was one of two Team USA [[Standard-bearer|flag-bearers]] for the [[2024 Summer Olympics opening ceremony|opening ceremony]] of the games, becoming the first male basketball player to receive the honor.<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 22, 2024 |title=NBA superstar James named USA's Olympic flagbearer |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/articles/c250z5rgwj3o |access-date=July 22, 2024 |website=BBC}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=July 22, 2024 |title=LeBron James to Serve as Flag Bearer for Team USA at Paris 2024 Opening Ceremony |url=https://www.usab.com/news/2024/07/lebron-james-to-serve-as-flag-bearer-for-team-usa-at-paris-2024-opening-ceremony |access-date=July 22, 2024 |website=USA Basketball}}</ref> James led the team in rebounds and assists, and recorded his second Olympic triple double,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Steph Curry, LeBron James fuel USA's comeback win over Serbia |url=https://www.nba.com/news/usa-serbia-paris-olympics |access-date=August 9, 2024 |website=NBA.com |language=en}}</ref> becoming the first player in Olympic history with two triple doubles.<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 8, 2024 |title=USA fight back from −17 to defeat Serbia in Semi-Finals |url=https://www.fiba.basketball/en/events/mens-olympic-basketball-tournament-paris-2024/news/usa-fight-back-from-17-to-defeat-serbia-in-semi-finals |access-date=August 10, 2024 |website=www.fiba.basketball |language=en}}</ref> Team USA won their fifth straight gold medal, defeating France 98–87 in the final game.<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 10, 2024 |title=Basketball: USA win men's gold, beating France 98–87 – Paris 2024 |url=https://olympics.com/en/paris-2024/live-updates/5c19d7a0-e32c-44e6-80fd-a2733b71bede |access-date=August 10, 2024 |website=olympics.com |language=en}}</ref> With averages of 14.2 points, 6.8 rebounds and 8.5 assists in the tournament, James was named the [[FIBA Men's Olympics MVP]] and was selected to the [[FIBA Men's Olympics All-Star Five]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fiba.basketball/en/events/mens-olympic-basketball-tournament-paris-2024/news/lebron-james-mvp-of-the-paris-2024-headlines-the-all-star-five |website=FIBA |access-date=August 11, 2024 |title=LeBron James MVP of the Paris 2024 headlines the All-Star Five |date=August 10, 2024}}</ref> James became the third male basketball player to win three gold medals at the Olympics.

==Player profile==
Standing {{convert|6|ft|9|in|m|2}} tall and weighing {{convert|250|lbs|kg|0}},<ref>{{Cite web |title=LeBron James |url=https://www.nba.com/player/2544/lebron-james |access-date=2026-03-07 |website=NBA}}</ref> James has played the majority of his career at the [[small forward]] and [[power forward]] positions,<ref name="Reference">{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.basketball-reference.com/players/j/jamesle01.html|title=LeBron James Stats|website=Basketball Reference|publisher=Sports Reference|date=June 12, 2004|access-date=April 25, 2024}}</ref> but he has also been deployed at other positions when necessary.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Simmons|first=Bill|title=LeBron Makes LeLeap|url=http://grantland.com/features/lebron-makes-leleap/|website=Grantland|date=June 22, 2012|access-date=June 22, 2012}}</ref> His playing style, which is athletic and versatile,<ref name="Goldsberry">{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Goldsberry|first=Kirk|title=The Evolution of King James|url=http://grantland.com/features/how-lebron-james-transformed-game-become-highly-efficient-scoring-machine/|website=Grantland|date=March 29, 2013|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> has drawn comparisons to [[Basketball Hall of Fame]] players [[Oscar Robertson]], [[Magic Johnson]] and [[Michael Jordan]].{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=DuPree|first=David|url=http://usatoday30.usatoday.com/sports/basketball/playoffs/2006-04-20-james-cover_x.htm|title=King James' next conquest|work=USA Today|date=April 21, 2006|access-date=August 21, 2006}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Davis|first=Nate|title=Jalen Rose, Warren Sapp scoff at notion of LeBron in NFL|url=http://content.usatoday.com/communities/thehuddle/post/2011/11/jalen-rose-warren-sapp-scoff-at-notion-of-lebron-james-playing-in-nfl/|newspaper=USA Today|access-date=June 23, 2012|date=November 17, 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |date=August 5, 2014 |title=Sports Illustrated's Fittest 50 |url=https://www.si.com/edge/photos/2014/08/05/sports-illustrated-fittest-50-athletes-sports |magazine=Sports Illustrated |access-date=August 10, 2014}}</ref>}}

===Offense===
As an 18-year-old rookie, James led the Cavaliers in scoring.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=2003–04 Cleveland Cavaliers Roster and Stats|url=https://www.basketball-reference.com/teams/CLE/2004.html|website=Basketball Reference|publisher=Sports Reference}}</ref> He holds numerous "youngest to" distinctions,<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|title=James receives 78 of 118 first-place votes|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/news/story?id=1786166|website=ESPN|access-date=December 22, 2021|date=April 21, 2004|agency=Associated Press}}</ref><ref name="usabio">{{#invoke:cite|web|publisher=USA Basketball|url=http://www.usabasketball.com/biosmen/lebron_james_bio.html|title=USA Basketball: LeBron James Bio|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070514045140/http://www.usabasketball.com/biosmen/lebron_james_bio.html|archive-date=May 14, 2007}}</ref> including being the youngest player to score 30,000 career points.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron James' path to 30,000 career regular-season points|url=http://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/22134348/lebron-james-path-30000-career-regular-season-points|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=September 15, 2018|date=January 2018}}</ref> During his first stint in Cleveland, James was primarily used as an on-ball [[point forward]], and although his shooting tendencies were perimeter-oriented,<ref name=Goldsberry/> he established himself as one of the best [[Slasher (basketball)|slashers]] and finishers in basketball.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Kim|first=Allen|date=October 8, 2010|title=NBA Power Rankings: Dwyane Wade and the Top 20 Slashers in the NBA|url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/485933-nba-power-rankings-dwyane-wade-and-the-top-20-slashers-in-the-nba|website=Bleacher Report|access-date=May 19, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Burton|first=Roy|date=March 30, 2012|title=Power Ranking the NBA's Most Reckless Slashers|url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/1125089-power-ranking-the-nbas-most-reckless-slashers|website=Bleacher Report|access-date=May 19, 2021}}</ref> His combination of speed and size often created matchup problems for opposing teams because James was capable of charging past larger defenders and overpowering smaller ones.<ref name="Evolution">{{cite magazine |last=Mahoney |first=Rob |date=December 7, 2016 |title=Then And Now: The Evolution Of LeBron James |url=https://www.si.com/nba/2016/12/07/lebron-james-cavaliers-heat-dwyane-wade-chris-bosh-kyrie-irving |magazine=Sports Illustrated |access-date=April 8, 2017}}</ref> James was frequently criticized for not having a reliable [[Jump shot (basketball)|jump shot]] or post game.{{Citation needed|date=March 2026}} Teams would try to exploit these weaknesses by forcing him to settle for three-pointers and long two-pointers, a strategy famously used by Spurs coach [[Gregg Popovich]] in the 2007 Finals, during which James scored on only 36 percent of his two-point field goal attempts, and on only 20 percent of his three-point attempts.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Zillgitt|first=Jeff|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nba/playoffs/2013/06/04/lebron-james-miami-heat-vs-san-antonio-spurs-2007-finals-cleveland-cavaliers/2390097/|title=LeBron James '50 times better' than in 2007 NBA Finals|newspaper=USA Today|access-date=April 8, 2017}}</ref>[[File:Lebronred.jpg|thumb|left|upright=0.7|James drives to the basket in March 2008. A deft finisher, he led the NBA in scoring and shooting percentage at the rim in 2013.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Goldsberry|first=Kirk|title=The 2012–13 CourtVision Awards: The Best Shooters|url=http://www.grantland.com/blog/the-triangle/post/_/id/68456/the-2012-13-courtvision-awards-the-best-shooters|website=Grantland|date=July 12, 2013|access-date=November 24, 2013}}</ref>]]In Miami, Heat coach [[Erik Spoelstra]] changed James's role to a more unconventional one.<ref name=Goldsberry/> James spent more time in [[Key (basketball)|the post]] and improved his shot selection and accuracy on jump shots.<ref name=Goldsberry/><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Haberstroh|first=Tom|title=Is LeBron James an elite shooter?|date=February 25, 2013|url=http://insider.espn.com/nba/story/_/page/PerDiem-130225/nba-lebron-james-shooting-star|work=ESPN|access-date=June 17, 2013}}{{subscription required}}</ref> He also learned how to work as an off-ball cutter in the Heat's "pass-happy" offense.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Lowe|first=Zach|title=The Miami Juggernaut|url=http://grantland.com/features/how-miami-heat-went-historic-winning-streak-came-dominate-league/|website=Grantland|date=March 26, 2013|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> With these improvements, James's overall scoring efficiency rose significantly.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Levy|first=Ian|title=What Drives LeBron James' Scoring Efficiency?|url=http://hardwoodparoxysm.com/2014/04/29/drives-lebron-james-scoring-efficiency/|publisher=Hardwood Paroxysm|access-date=April 8, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170409111401/http://hardwoodparoxysm.com/2014/04/29/drives-lebron-james-scoring-efficiency/|archive-date=April 9, 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref> During this time, ESPN's Tom Haberstroh called James's free-throw shooting his biggest weakness.<ref name=Haber>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Haberstroh|first=Tom|title=Miami Heat: 2013–14 roster (Subscription required)|date=September 18, 2013|url=http://insider.espn.com/nba/preview2013/story/_/page/2013-14-mia-preview/miami-heat-player-profiles|work=ESPN Insider|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref>

In 2015 and 2016, James began to experience subtle age-related declines in productivity,<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Shoals |first=Bethlehem |title=LeBron James Is Underrated and Overlooked |url=https://www.gq.com/story/lebron-james-is-underrated-and-overlooked |magazine=GQ |access-date=April 9, 2016}}</ref> posting his lowest scoring averages since his rookie season.<ref name="Reference" /><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Engelmann|first=Jeremias|title=NBA has co-MVPs this season|date=April 8, 2016|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/insider/story/_/id/15160735/nba-co-mvps-season|work=ESPN Insider|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> His shooting also temporarily regressed, and he briefly ranked as the NBA's worst high-volume shooter from outside [[Key (basketball)|the key]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Yuscavage |first=Chris |date=December 29, 2015 |url=https://www.complex.com/sports/2015/12/lebron-james-worst-shooter-nba-this-season |title=LeBron James Is the Worst Shooter in the NBA So Far This Season |magazine=Complex |access-date=January 7, 2022}}</ref> Despite these changes, he remained an elite offensive player who beat defenses with body control, strength, and varying attack speeds.<ref name="Evolution" />

For most of his career, James has controlled the offense as the primary ball handler on his team.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Windhorst|first=Brian|title=LeBron James takes control of the Lakers|date=November 28, 2018|website=ESPN|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/25384727/lebron-james-takes-control-lakers|access-date=November 28, 2018}}</ref> His playmaking ability is generally considered one of his premier skills, and some analysts rank him among the greatest passers in NBA history.<ref name="Lowe2">{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Lowe|first=Zach|title=The Decision 2.0: OK, What's Next?|url=http://grantland.com/the-triangle/lebron-james-cleveland-cavaliers-aftermath-miami-heat/|website=Grantland|date=July 11, 2014|access-date=July 13, 2014|archive-date=December 14, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211214091730/http://grantland.com/the-triangle/lebron-james-cleveland-cavaliers-aftermath-miami-heat/|url-status=live}}</ref> By exploiting his size, vision, and the attention he garners from opposing defenses,<ref name="Rosenberg">{{cite magazine |last=Rosenberg |first=Michael |title=Don't hate LeBron, enjoy him; he's most gifted player in NBA history |url=https://www.si.com/more-sports/2012/05/21/lebron |magazine=Sports Illustrated |access-date=December 22, 2021 |date=May 21, 2012}}</ref> he creates easy points for his teammates with precise assists.<ref name="Mahoney">{{cite magazine |last=Mahoney |first=Rob |title=The Case For: LeBron James as Most Valuable Player |url=https://www.si.com/nba/2013/04/16/lebron-james-mvp-nba-2013 |magazine=Sports Illustrated |access-date=December 22, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130527070601/http://nba.si.com/2013/04/16/lebron-james-mvp-nba-2013/ |archive-date=May 27, 2013}}</ref> James executes unconventional passes, including after leaving his feet and through defensive traffic.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Windhorst|first=Brian|title=LeBron James' unprecedented season of sharing has arrived|date=November 29, 2016|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/18159427/why-lebron-james-cooking-more-dishes|work=ESPN|access-date=January 15, 2017}}</ref> His uncanny tendency to find an open player has pushed opposing teams to incorporate elements of [[zone defense]] into their strategies.<ref name="Evolution" /> Early in his career, James was criticized for overpassing in pressure situations, in particular for passing instead of shooting in the waning seconds of close games;<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Morre|first=Matt|title=Heat 93, Pacers 91: LeBron is clutch, then not clutch, clutch enough?|date=March 10, 2012|work=CBS Sports|url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/heat-93-pacers-91-lebron-is-clutch-then-not-clutch-clutch-enough/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130407000005/http://www.cbssports.com/nba/blog/eye-on-basketball/17717241/heat-93-pacers-91-lebron-is-clutch-then-not-clutch-clutch-enough|archive-date=April 7, 2013|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Jackson|first=Scoop|title=LeBron's stomach-turning stigma|date=March 8, 2012|publisher=[[ESPN]]|url=https://www.espn.com/espn/commentary/story/_/page/jackson-120308/lebron-james-passing-last-second-shots-earns-long-lasting-stigma|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120309191029/http://espn.go.com/espn/commentary/story/_/page/jackson-120308/lebron-james-passing-last-second-shots-earns-long-lasting-stigma|archive-date=March 9, 2012|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> however, as his career progressed, James's [[Clutch (sports)|clutch]] performance was viewed more favorably.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Paine|first=Neil|title=LeBron May Be The Most Clutch Playoff Shooter Of His Generation|url=http://fivethirtyeight.com/datalab/lebron-may-be-the-most-clutch-playoff-shooter-of-his-generation/|website=FiveThirtyEight|date=May 11, 2015|access-date=May 22, 2015}}</ref>

===Defense===
[[File:LeBron James (40626830701).jpg|thumb|James defending against [[Joe Harris (basketball)|Joe Harris]] in February 2018]]
At the beginning of his NBA career, James was considered a poor defensive player,<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron against the all-time greats|date=March 2012|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/page/5-on-5-120301/nba-lebron-james-all-time-greats|work=ESPN|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> but he improved steadily over the years. In 2009, he demonstrated proficiency at the [[chase-down block]].<ref name="Abrams">{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Abrams|first=Jonathan|title=On Defense, James Is Closer Than He Appears|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2010/05/06/sports/basketball/06cavs.html?_r=0|newspaper=The New York Times|access-date=June 11, 2013|date=May 5, 2010}}</ref> In Miami, he developed into a more versatile defensive player, and the Heat relied on him to guard all five positions.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Haberstroh|first=Tom|title='Point center' LeBron James fourth in DPOY|date=May 2, 2012|url=https://www.espn.com/blog/truehoop/miamiheat/post/_/id/13790/point-center-lebron-james-fourth-in-dpoy|work=ESPN|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> Between 2012 and 2016, he was ranked among the top three defenders in the NBA by general managers, and was named the best perimeter defender in the league ahead of the [[2014–15 NBA season|2014–15 season]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=NBA GM Survey: 2014–15 edition |url=https://www.nba.com/news/nba-gm-survey-2014-15 |access-date=December 20, 2024 |website=nba.com}}</ref> Along with [[Shane Battier]] and Dwyane Wade, Miami used James in an ultra-aggressive defensive scheme,<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Lowe|first=Zach|title=Lights, Cameras, Revolution|url=http://grantland.com/features/the-toronto-raptors-sportvu-cameras-nba-analytical-revolution/|website=Grantland|date=March 19, 2013|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> with James [[Glossary of basketball terms#cheat|cheating]] off the ball to help out inside or to get into rebounding position.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Harper|first=Zach|title=LeBron James' defensive assignment allows versatility for Miami Heat|url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-defensive-assignment-allows-versatility-for-miami-heat/|work=CBS Sports|date=May 23, 2013 |access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> Beginning in 2014, some analysts saw a regression in his defensive impact, stemming from a lack of effort and expected age-related declines.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Haberstroh|first=Tom|title=Who's the real plus-minus MVP?|date=April 9, 2014|url=http://insider.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/10754836/nba-does-real-plus-minus-say-league-most-valuable-player|work=ESPN Insider|access-date=December 22, 2021|url-access=subscription}}</ref><ref name="WPDecline">{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Partnow|first=Seth|title=Here's proof LeBron James is exiting the prime of his career|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/fancy-stats/wp/2016/01/05/heres-proof-lebron-james-is-exiting-the-prime-of-his-career/|newspaper=The Washington Post|access-date=August 7, 2016}}</ref> During his second stint in Cleveland, James's defense progressively declined. After missed drives on offense, he often dawdled back on defense while complaining to the referees; he provided less help [[Glossary of basketball terms#off the ball|off the ball]], and was less aggressive in [[switch (basketball)|switching]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Duncan|first=Nate|title=NBA No-Defense Team: Carmelo Anthony, Enes Kanter and Regular Season LeBron James get the big honors|date=June 12, 2018|work=The Athletic|url=https://theathletic.com/383038/2018/06/12/nba-no-defense-team-carmelo-anthony-enes-kanter-and-regular-season-lebron-james-get-the-big-honors/|url-access=subscription|access-date=March 5, 2019|quote=His regular-season work has increasingly lagged during his Cleveland years, but even as recently as last season the overall numbers were solid.}}</ref> James himself admitted to taking plays off at times, referring to this approach as "chill mode".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Pelton|first=Kevin|date=December 31, 2014|title=LeBron's 'chill mode' hurting Cavs|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/12102220/nba-why-lebron-james-chill-mode-hurting-cleveland-cavaliers|access-date=April 8, 2017|publisher=[[ESPN]]}}</ref> He eventually developed a reputation for raising his defensive impact in the playoffs, which some analysts referred to as "Playoff LeBron".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Alamar|first=Ben|title=It's defense that makes 'Playoff LeBron' a thing|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/23027889/playoff-impact-lebron-james-felt-mainly-defense-nba|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=September 15, 2018|date=April 6, 2018}}</ref>

==Legacy==
[[File:Lebron wizards 2017 (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright=0.81|left|James with the Cavaliers in 2017. According to NBA analyst [[Brian Windhorst]], who has covered James since high school, "No one has ever had as much hype as James has had to live up to, and James has delivered on every last drop."<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Windhorst|first=Brian|title=All-Time #NBArank: LeBron No. 3|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/page/nbarank3/all-nbarank-3|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=October 14, 2018|date=February 10, 2016}}</ref>]]

James left high school as one of the most [[Media circus|hyped]] prospects in NBA history.{{efn|See Ryan Jones,<ref name="Jones2003"/>{{rp|142}} [[Jay Bilas]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Bilas|first=Jay|title=Did 'LeBron Mania' go too far?|url=http://www.espn.com/columns/bilas_jay/1477784.html|publisher=[[ESPN]]|date=December 17, 2002|access-date=August 6, 2017}}</ref> [[Chris Broussard]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Broussard|first=Chris|title=James Answers the Hype with Standout Debut|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2003/10/30/sports/basketball-james-answers-hype-with-standout-debut.html|newspaper=The New York Times|date=October 30, 2003|access-date=August 6, 2017}}</ref> [[Sam Smith (sportswriter)|Sam Smith]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Smith|first=Sam|title=Hype over LeBron doesn't match Alcindor's|url=http://a.espncdn.com/nba/columns/smith_sam/1475855.html|publisher=[[ESPN]]|date=December 12, 2003|access-date=August 6, 2017}}</ref> and [[Chad Ford]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Ford|first=Chad|title=Top 25 draft prospects since 2000|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/draft2014/insider/story/_/id/11099139/nba-draft-lebron-james-leads-rank-top-25-draft-prospects-last-15-years|publisher=[[ESPN]]|date=June 18, 2014|access-date=August 6, 2017|website=ESPN Insider}}</ref>}} Upon entering the league, he made an immediate impact and was voted Rookie of the Year in his debut season.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=NBA Rookie of the Year Award Winners|url=http://www.nba.com/history/awards/rookie-of-the-year|website=NBA.com|access-date=October 14, 2018}}</ref> As of 2024, James has been named to 21 All-NBA Teams, including 13 times to the First Team, which are both NBA records.<ref name="Quinn 2021"/> His four MVP awards are matched only by Michael Jordan, Kareem Abdul-Jabbar, Wilt Chamberlain, and [[Bill Russell]]; James and Russell are the only players to win four MVP awards in a five-year span.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=LeBron takes 2013 Kia Most Valuable Player award|url=http://www.nba.com/2013/news/05/05/lebron-2013-mvp-award/index.html?ls=iref:nbahpt3b|website=NBA.com|access-date=May 5, 2013|date=May 5, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130507235207/http://www.nba.com/2013/news/05/05/lebron-2013-mvp-award/index.html?ls=iref:nbahpt3b|archive-date=May 7, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref> James has also won four Finals MVP Awards, which is the second-most all-time,<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=NBA Finals MVP Award Winners|url=http://www.nba.com/history/awards/finals-mvp|website=NBA.com|access-date=October 14, 2018}}</ref> and earned All-Defensive honors every season from 2009 to 2014.<ref name=Reference/> While James has never won the Defensive Player of the Year Award, he has finished second in the voting twice and lists it among his goals.<ref name=DPOTY09/><ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Wallace|first=Michael|title=LeBron James wins 4th MVP award|date=May 5, 2013|publisher=[[ESPN]]|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/playoffs/2013/story/_/id/9244504/lebron-james-miami-heat-1-vote-shy-unanimous-mvp-honor|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130505201808/http://espn.go.com/nba/playoffs/2013/story/_/id/9244504/lebron-james-miami-heat-1-vote-shy-unanimous-mvp-honor|archive-date=May 5, 2013|url-status=live}}</ref> His teams have appeared in the Finals ten times and won four championships; his 10 Finals appearances are tied for third all-time.{{efn|Tied with Abdul-Jabbar behind [[Bill Russell]] (12) and [[Sam Jones (basketball, born 1933)|Sam Jones]] (11) of the Celtics<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|title=LeBron James one win away from history: 10th NBA Finals appearance|date=September 26, 2020|website=NBC Sports|agency=Associated Press|url=https://nba.nbcsports.com/2020/09/26/lebron-james-one-win-away-from-history-10th-nba-finals-apperance/|access-date=October 9, 2020}}</ref>}} Some analysts have criticized him for not having a better Finals record, while others have countered that James usually performed well but his team was defeated by superior competition.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Paine|first=Neil|title=Where This Year's Cavs Rank Among LeBron's NBA Finals Supporting Casts|url=http://fivethirtyeight.com/datalab/where-this-years-cavs-rank-among-lebrons-nba-finals-supporting-casts/|website=FiveThirtyEight|access-date=August 7, 2016|date=June 1, 2015}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Haberstroh|first=Tom|title=LeBron's 2–4 Finals record is one of his greatest achievements|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/insider/story/_/id/15882307/what-lebron-james-losing-nba-finals-record-really-means-nba|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=August 7, 2016|date=June 2, 2016}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Lowe|first=Zach|title=The Rematch: An NBA Finals preview|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/15888230/this-matchup-cavs-warriors-what-saw-2015|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=August 7, 2016|date=June 2, 2016}}</ref>}}

Based on his career longevity and on-court performances, sports publications have regarded James as one of the greatest basketball players in history,{{efn|See ''[[Sports Illustrated]]'' (ranked 5th in 2016),<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=McCullum|first=Jack|title=SI's 50 greatest players in NBA history|url=https://www.si.com/nba/2016/02/09/michael-jordan-lebron-james-stephen-curry-nba-greatest|access-date=October 14, 2018|date=February 8, 2016|magazine=Sports Illustrated}}</ref> [[ESPN]] (ranked 3rd in 2016 and 2nd in 2020),<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=All-Time #NBArank: Counting down the greatest players ever|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/page/nbarankalltime/greatest-players-ever|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=May 27, 2017|date=March 3, 2016}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Ranking the top 74 NBA players of all time: Nos. 10–1|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/29105801/ranking-top-74-nba-players-all-nos-10-1|website=ESPN.com|date=May 13, 2020|access-date=April 3, 2022}}</ref> [[CBS Sports]] (ranked 2nd in 2017),<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=CBS Sports' 50 greatest NBA players of all time: Where do LeBron, Curry rank?|url=http://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/cbs-sports-50-greatest-nba-players-of-all-time-where-do-lebron-curry-rank/|work=CBS Sports|access-date=February 18, 2017|date=February 17, 2017}}</ref> [[Fox Sports]] (ranked 2nd in 2017),<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Lynch|first=Andrew|title=Ranking the 25 greatest players in NBA history|url=http://www.foxsports.com/nba/gallery/ranking-the-25-greatest-players-in-nba-history-100716|work=Fox Sports|access-date=October 14, 2018|date=December 25, 2017}}</ref> ''[[Slam (magazine)|Slam]]'' (ranked 2nd in 2018),<ref>{{cite magazine |title=Top 100: The Greatest Players of All Time |magazine=Slam |last=Page |first=Dennis S. |date=February 23, 2018}}</ref> and ''[[Bleacher Report]]'' (ranked 2nd in 2019).<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Bailey|first=Andy|title=Bleacher Report's All-Time Player Rankings: NBA's Top 50 Revealed|url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/2854727-bleacher-reports-all-time-player-rankings-nbas-top-50-revealed|website=Bleacher Report|access-date=March 31, 2020|date=September 26, 2019}}</ref>}} and he was named the Associated Press Male Athlete of the Decade for the 2010s.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|title=LeBron James named AP top male athlete of decade|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/28389041/lebron-james-named-ap-top-male-athlete-decade|website=ESPN|access-date=October 31, 2020|date=December 29, 2019|agency=Associated Press}}</ref> His high rankings have resulted in frequent debates about whether James or Michael Jordan is the greatest player of all time.{{efn|name=GOAT debate}} In a 2016 interview with ''Sports Illustrated'', James said he was hoping to surpass Jordan as the greatest player.<ref name="Quinn">{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Quinn|first=Sam|title=LeBron James' quest to catch Michael Jordan faces an obstacle both utterly unparalleled and strangely familiar|work=CBS Sports|date=March 25, 2020|access-date=April 1, 2020|url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-quest-to-catch-michael-jordan-faces-an-obstacle-both-utterly-unparalleled-and-strangely-familiar/}}</ref> In February 2018, ''[[The Ringer (website)|The Ringer]]'' spent an entire week devoted to both players, with [[Bill Simmons]] ultimately concluding that Jordan was still ahead.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Jordan-LeBron Week|url=https://www.theringer.com/nba/2018/2/20/17029830/lebron-vs-jordan-week|website=The Ringer|access-date=October 14, 2018|date=February 19, 2018}}</ref> James has ranked second behind Jordan in polls, the results of which show a strong correlation with the age of respondents, as older voters more often choose Jordan.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref name="Manrique">{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Manrique|first=Bruno|title=NBA players overwhelmingly vote Michael Jordan as the GOAT over LeBron James, Kobe Bryant|work=ClutchPoints|date=April 8, 2019|access-date=April 6, 2020|url=https://clutchpoints.com/nba-news-players-overwhelmingly-vote-michael-jordan-goat-over-lebron-james-kobe-bryant/}}</ref><ref name="Parrish">{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Parrish|first=Gary|title=Candid Coaches: Who's the real GOAT – Michael Jordan or LeBron James?|work=CBS Sports|date=August 31, 2018|access-date=April 1, 2020|url=https://www.cbssports.com/college-basketball/news/candid-coaches-whos-the-real-goat-michael-jordan-or-lebron-james/}}</ref><ref name="Davis">{{#invoke:cite|news|last1=Davis|first1=Scott|last2=Hickey|first2=Walt|last3=Yutong|first3=Yuan|title=Most Americans think Michael Jordan is the 'GOAT' over LeBron James, and it's not even close|website=Business Insider|date=March 18, 2019|access-date=April 1, 2020|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/jordan-lebron-goat-debate-americans-jordan-2019-3}}</ref>}} ''[[Business Insider]]'' stated that the data "would suggest that younger, more-engaged NBA fans lean toward James, as he's still playing" while older generations "who watched Jordan play and tune in less today lean toward Jordan."<ref name="d716">{{cite web | last=Brady | first=Alex | title=Recency Bias and Its Footing in the NBA GOAT Debate | website=The Georgetown Voice | date=2020-10-24 | url=https://georgetownvoice.com/2020/10/24/recency-bias-nba-goat/ | access-date=2025-08-14}}</ref><ref name="Davis" /> Referring to James as the best challenger to Jordan's status as the greatest player, Sam Quinn of CBS Sports stated that "in the rings-obsessed basketball discourse", Jordan having more titles and an "unblemished Finals record holds significant weight".<ref name="Quinn" />

In addition to praising James's on-court accomplishments, analysts have also noted his influence on player empowerment throughout the NBA, which stemmed from his willingness to change teams during free agency. Ben Golliver of ''[[The Washington Post]]'' said that James's move to the Heat in 2010 "defined a decade of player movement", and that he "fundamentally flipped the power balance between stars and their organizations."<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Golliver|first=Ben|title=LeBron James' 'Decision' defined a decade of player movement|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/sports/2020/07/06/lebron-james-the-decision-impact/|access-date=October 31, 2020|newspaper=The Washington Post|date=July 6, 2020}}{{subscription required}}</ref> Players have also remarked on his influence, such as Warriors forward [[Draymond Green]], who reflected: "We've taken control of our destiny. And I think a lot of people hate that ... I think the doors that he's opened for athletes and especially basketball players is his biggest accomplishment."<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Kaskey-Blomain|first=Michael|title=Warriors' Draymond Green credits Lakers' LeBron James for helping to empower NBA players|url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/warriors-draymond-green-credits-lakers-lebron-james-for-helping-to-empower-nba-players/|work=CBS Sports|access-date=October 31, 2020|date=September 16, 2019}}</ref> Multiple current and former NBA players have suggested James's free agency decisions catalyzed the league-wide trend in "[[Superteams in the NBA|superteams]]" in the 21st century.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rohrbach |first=Ben |date=June 6, 2017 |title=Kevin Durant: LeBron James 'paved the way' for this Warriors super-team |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/kevin-durant-lebron-james-paved-way-warriors-super-team-202638207.html |access-date=July 1, 2024 |website=Yahoo! Sports |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Starjacki |first=Will |date=April 27, 2021 |title=Julius Erving takes a subtle jab at LeBron James for creating superteams |url=https://www.basketballnetwork.net/latest-news/julius-erving-takes-a-subtle-jab-at-lebron-james-for-creating-superteams |access-date=July 1, 2024 |website=Basketball Network |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Nelson |first=Cory |date=July 18, 2022 |title=Shaquille O'Neal Blames LeBron James For 'Superteam' Concept |url=https://www.si.com/nba/heat/miami-news/shaquille-oneal-blames-lebron-james-for-superteam-concept |access-date=July 1, 2024 |magazine=Sports Illustrated |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Barrasso |first=Justin |date=June 10, 2021 |title=Charles Barkley: 'I Root Against All Superteams' |url=https://www.si.com/nba/2021/06/10/charles-barkley-nba-playoffs-nets-superteam |access-date=July 1, 2024 |magazine=Sports Illustrated |language=en-us}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Axson |first=Scooby |date=June 16, 2017 |title=LeBron James: I didn't start superteams |url=https://www.si.com/nba/2017/06/16/lebron-james-address-superteams-claims |access-date=July 1, 2024 |magazine=Sports Illustrated |language=en-us}}</ref>}}

===Public image===
James is often considered by fellow NBA players and the media to be the "face of the NBA", frequently alongside [[Golden State Warriors]] superstar [[Stephen Curry]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Vardon|first=Joe|title=LeBron James is the 'face' of the NBA, but is Stephen Curry next?|date=February 15, 2015|url=https://www.cleveland.com/cavs/2015/02/lebron_james_stephen_curry_fac.html|newspaper=[[The Plain Dealer]]|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |date=June 2, 2016 |title=Stephen Curry annoyed by 'face of the NBA' debate |url=https://www.si.com/nba/2016/06/02/stephen-curry-lebron-james-face-nba-warriors-cavaliers |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190119121234/https://www.si.com/nba/2016/06/02/stephen-curry-lebron-james-face-nba-warriors-cavaliers |archive-date=January 19, 2019 |access-date=January 17, 2019 |magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]] |author=SI Wire}}</ref> In 2014, James reportedly asked NBA commissioner [[Adam Silver]] to increase the duration of the All-Star break, and it was extended the following season.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Feldman|first=Dan|title=LeBron James reportedly asked Adam Silver for longer All-Star break, fewer back-to-backs|date=January 30, 2015|url=https://nba.nbcsports.com/2015/01/30/lebron-james-reportedly-asked-adam-silver-for-longer-all-star-break-fewer-back-to-backs/|publisher=NBC Sports|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> On February 13, 2015, James was elected the first vice president of the [[National Basketball Players Association]] (NBPA).<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Pollakoff|first=Brett|title=Report: LeBron James elected Vice President of NBA Players Association|date=February 13, 2015|url=https://nba.nbcsports.com/2015/02/13/report-lebron-james-elected-vice-resident-of-nba-players-association/|publisher=NBC Sports|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> Throughout the 2010s, James was usually ranked as the best player in the NBA each season by ESPN and ''Sports Illustrated''.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Windhorst|first=Brian|title=LeBron James is still the undefeated champ of #NBArank|url=http://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/20703687/cleveland-cavaliers-lebron-james-remains-undefeated-champ-nbarank|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=September 15, 2018|date=September 15, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=SI's Top 100 NBA Players of 2019: How Long Will LeBron James Remain on Top|url=https://www.si.com/nba/video/2018/09/13/top-100-nba-players-how-long-will-lebron-james-remain-top|access-date=September 15, 2018|date=September 13, 2018|magazine=Sports Illustrated}}</ref>

Throughout his career, James has been ranked by ''Forbes'' as one of the world's most influential athletes,{{efn|Such as in 2010<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://www.forbes.com/2010/04/21/lance-armstrong-endorsements-business-sports-influential-athletes.html |title=The Most Influential Athletes |magazine=Forbes |date=April 21, 2010 |access-date=January 11, 2022}}</ref> and 2013<ref>{{cite magazine |date=May 6, 2013 |title=Most Influential Athletes 2013 |url=https://www.forbes.com/pictures/eddf45kkml/lebron-james-4/ |magazine=Forbes |access-date=July 27, 2013 |last=Van Riper |first=Tom}}</ref>}} and has been listed by ''[[Time (magazine)|Time]]'' as one of the [[Time 100|100 most influential people in the world]].<ref>{{cite news |title=LeBron James is one of Time's 100 Most Influential People again |url=https://www.beaconjournal.com/story/news/local/2019/04/17/lebron-james-is-one-time/5415499007/ |access-date=January 1, 2024 |work=Akron Beacon Journal |date=April 17, 2019}}</ref> During his first stint with the Cavaliers, James was adored by local fans, and [[Sherwin-Williams]] displayed a giant Nike-produced banner of James at its world headquarters.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Cho|first=Janet|title=Sherwin-Williams replaces LeBron poster with Cleveland skyline|date=October 27, 2010|url=https://www.cleveland.com/business/2010/10/sherwin-williams_replaces_lebr.html|website=[[Cleveland.com]]|access-date=December 1, 2012}}</ref> Despite their affection for James, some Cleveland fans were irritated when he wore a Yankees cap at a [[Cleveland Indians]] baseball game against the [[New York Yankees]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Briggs |first=David |date=October 5, 2007 |title=LeBron spurns Tribe, sports Yanks cap |url=http://mlb.mlb.com/content/printer_friendly/mlb/y2007/m10/d04/c2250946.jsp |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230301195631/http://mlb.mlb.com/content/printer_friendly/mlb/y2007/m10/d04/c2250946.jsp |archive-date=March 1, 2023 |website=MLB}}</ref> Following his actions during the 2010 free agency period and ''The Decision'', James was listed as one of the most disliked athletes in the United States.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Van Riper |first=Tom |date=February 7, 2012 |title=America's Most Disliked Athletes |url=https://www.forbes.com/pictures/eddf45fkhi/lebron-james-2/ |magazine=Forbes |access-date=January 11, 2022}}</ref> By 2013, his image had mostly recovered and he was reported by ESPN as the most popular player in the NBA for the second time in his career.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Rovell|first=Darren|title=LeBron James NBA's most popular|date=July 26, 2013|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/truehoop/miamiheat/story/_/id/9512608/poll-shows-lebron-james-passes-kobe-bryant-nba-most-popular-player|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> In 2014, James was named the most popular male athlete in America by the Harris Poll.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Harper|first=Zach|title=LeBron James is finally the most popular male athlete in America|url=https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-is-finally-the-most-popular-male-athlete-in-america/|work=CBS Sports|date=July 17, 2014 |access-date=December 22, 2021}}</ref> He has led the league in jersey sales six times.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last=Rovell|first=Darren|title=LeBron James tops jersey sale|date=April 17, 2014|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/10795792/lebron-james-miami-heat-tops-nba-jersey-sales|publisher=[[ESPN]]|access-date=April 27, 2014}}</ref> As of June 2023, James is the [[Most followed users on Instagram|most followed basketball player on Instagram]], with over 155 million followers.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last1=Sprung |first1=Shlomo |title=The Most Popular NBA Players on Instagram |url=https://boardroom.tv/the-most-popular-nba-players-on-instagram/ |website=boardroom.tv |date=June 16, 2023 |access-date=August 17, 2023}}</ref>

